Derivation
  This renderer is derived from published footage plus public, established
  technique -- DDA traversal, perpendicular depth, floor casting, a depth
  buffer. No third-party source was consulted at any point. The full
  provenance audit lives in the development repository, along with the
  standing rule that nobody who writes code there may read the reference
  project's source, including to check whether it matches.

Billboard animation
  217 animated billboard loops ship in index.html. SEVEN are drawn by this
  project. The other 210 are TRANSFORMED from third-party footage retrieved
  through the Giphy API: cover-cropped to a 30x40 cell grid, re-rendered
  against an 82-glyph set, quantised to nine ink coverage rungs and a
  14-family hue plane, and cut to 32 frames. No pixel of an original
  survives; what ships is a per-cell index into this project's own glyph set
  and palette.

  ATTRIBUTION.md credits every one of the 210 -- creator, Giphy id, title and
  a link to the source. 185 have a named uploader, 25 do not and are marked
  as such. 127 distinct creators are represented. In the city itself, looking
  at a billboard and pressing E names the loop and its creator.

  No rights are claimed over the source works. The MIT licence above covers
  this project's own code and generated content, NOT the underlying works.
  If you are a creator listed in ATTRIBUTION.md and would rather not be, open
  an issue and the loop will be removed. A build of the same city carrying
  ZERO third-party animation is generated by the development repository, so
  nothing here depends on any particular loop.
